{"name":"Warp Drive","hex":"#eaf2f1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warp drive","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A technological device that warps spacetime to enable movement through space in a non-Newtonian manner.","An engine that allows a vessel to travel faster than light by manipulating spacetime to bypass Einstein's restrictive light barrier."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warp_drive"}],"entries":[{"title":"Warp Drive","blocks":[{"text":"Warp Drive is a short street in Sterling, Virginia, United States. Originally named Steeplechase Drive, it is located in an industrial park off Atlantic Boulevard, and primarily serves as the address for Northrop Grumman Innovation Systems, an aerospace company. The street ends at a circle where an off-ramp from Virginia State Highway 28 joins from the opposite direction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/2014-08-22_14_04_24_View_north_along_Sully_Road_%28Virginia_State_Route_28%29_at_the_Warp_Drive_exit_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/330px-2014-08-22_14_04_24_View_north_along_Sully_Road_%28Virginia_State_Route_28%29_at_the_Warp_Drive_exit_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_Drive"},{"title":"Warp drive","blocks":[{"text":"A warp drive or a drive enabling space warp is a fictional superluminal spacecraft propulsion system in many science fiction works, most notably Star Trek, and a subject of ongoing real-life physics research. The general concept of \"warp drive\" was introduced by John W. Campbell in his 1957 novel Islands of Space and was popularized by the Star Trek series. Its closest real-life equivalent is the Alcubierre drive, a theoretical solution of the field equations of general relativity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Warp_drive_starship.png/330px-Warp_drive_starship.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_drive"},{"title":"Warp (terminal)","blocks":[{"text":"Warp is an open-source terminal emulator written in Rust available for macOS, Windows and Linux. Notable features include Warp AI for command suggestions and code generation, Warp Drive for sharing commands and runbooks across teams, and an IDE-like editor with text selection and cursor positioning."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warp_(terminal)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_%28Atlantic_Boulevard%29_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_%28Atlantic_Boulevard%29_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_%28Atlantic_Boulevard%29_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/1280px-2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_%28Atlantic_Boulevard%29_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_%28Atlantic_Boulevard%29_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_%28Atlantic_Boulevard%29_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Warp Drive viewed from Atlantic Boulevard","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2018-07-29_14_27_34_View_west_along_Warp_Drive_at_Virginia_State_Route_1902_(Atlantic_Boulevard)_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/1280px-2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg/500px-2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Northrop Grumman facility entrance sign using the street name","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2018-07-29_14_24_37_Sign_at_the_entrance_to_the_Northrop_Grumman_Space_Center_at_Warp_Drive_along_Atlantic_Boulevard_in_Sterling%2C_Loudoun_County%2C_Virginia.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}